RECAST training

This repository includes code and task semantics from these sources:

1. RLSD (Self-Distilled RLVR), commit
   aca313b978de4fb3a509ddf1831bf61fe597a2eb.
   The veRL/Ray/FSDP/vLLM runtime in `verl/` starts from that release.
   https://github.com/iie-ycx/RLSD/tree/aca313b978de4fb3a509ddf1831bf61fe597a2eb

2. Open-o3-Video, commit
   4797fd1adfd261eea821e0fcb57c876afdbc0362.
   Student prompts, STGR task semantics, reward scoring and vision processing
   use this Apache-2.0 release. RECAST adds its spatial-matching options and
   the video decoder settings used by the training loader.
   https://github.com/marinero4972/Open-o3-Video

3. MeSD (Multi-Evidence Self-Distillation for VideoLLM).
   RECAST shares evidence-conditioned prompt construction and training
   utilities with MeSD.
   https://github.com/WhiteVentral/MeSD-code

4. VISD / Video_OPSD, commit
   c3d54b2006c31c196ec4c5e7ab562999263c5f58.
   The original RECAST training implementation follows its reward profile,
   no-feedback privileged replay, top-k token discrepancy, EMA teacher and
   curriculum settings. It is credited here as method provenance.
   https://github.com/Koreyoshi01/VISD

Original copyright notices and license headers are retained in derived source
files. Model weights, training annotations and media have their own terms.
